    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68787" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μόρῠχος</span></b> , ὁ, epith.
		of dionysus in Sicily, from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μορύσσω</span>,
		because his face was <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>smeared</i> with wine lees at the vintage: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μωρότερος Μορύχου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sophr.
					94
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj. only in Adv.
			
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μορυχώτερον</span>
			<i>more obscurely</i>, v. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				987a10
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
			</span></i> ad <i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i> c.</div>
